    "title": "Heavy police presence spotted in Berwick - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julia Priest ,\n1 hours ago\nBERWICK, COLUMBIA COUNTY (WBRE/WYOU) — 28/22 News was there as there was a large presence of police activity in Columbia County Wednesday night.\nColumbia County officials told 28/22 News the area of East 3rd and Pine Streets was shut down Wednesday night for a reported police incident.\n28/22 News Reporter Avery Nape was there in Berwick with a large police presence responding to the incident.\nPolice say a man was inside his home, armed and threatening to hurt himself.\nBerwick Police Chief Reagan Rafferty told 28/22 News the man was inside the home along East 3rd Street.\nThe original call went out from a family member saying the man was armed and intending to harm himself.\nWilkes University issues warning about financial shortfall Officers from the Columbia Montour SWAT team were on scene as negotiators attempted to talk him down for around four and a half hours.\nOfficers lined the streets with their rifles drawn, an armored vehicle could be seen in front of the home, and a drone was also deployed.\nThe scene is now cleared, and Chief Rafferty told 28/22 News they made the decision to clear after determining the man was not a threat to the public and was only intending to harm himself.\nThis is a developing story, and 28/22 News will provide updates as new information is made available.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to 28/22 News.\n1",
